<Layout title="Contact Koursea Blog" description="Contact the Koursea Blog editorial team about corrections, sources, partnerships or reader questions.">
  <article class="page prose"><p class="eyebrow">CONTACT</p><h1>Corrections and reader questions are welcome.</h1><p class="lead">Send clear details so our editorial team can review your request efficiently.</p><h2>Editorial corrections</h2><p>If a fare, policy, business detail or link has changed, email <a href="mailto:hello@koursea.com">hello@koursea.com</a> with the article URL, the passage concerned and a current official source where possible.</p><h2>General inquiries</h2><p>For partnerships, permissions or feedback, use the same address and include “Koursea Blog” in the subject line. We do not provide emergency, legal or medical consultation. Travelers in Korea can call 1330 for multilingual tourism assistance, 112 for police, or 119 for fire and medical emergencies.</p><h2>Response expectations</h2><p>We review messages in English or Korean. Response times vary, and submitting information does not guarantee publication or a listing.</p></article>
</Layout>
